; SmallBarn — NEW PlaceableDefinition (content-variety pass Task 3, 2026-08-26). One of 8
; brand-new farm buildings. See project/assets/buildings/small_barn/SmallBarn.tscn for the
; asset-level header (source, license, texture audit, measured-scale reasoning).
;
; NO DESIGN DOC STATES ANY OF THIS ITEM'S VALUES. cost = 15, footprint = Vector2i(2, 2)
; are FIRST-PASS PROPOSALS sourced only from House's own stated 1x1 baseline (~15 Wood
; — buildings.md) — FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF, same as every other new farm building in
; this batch. allowed_terrain = ["grass"] (matching House) is this task's own explicit
; uniform choice, not sourced from a design doc row.
;
; fact_text is Content Pipeline step 5 (content-writer's job) — left as PLACEHOLDER, the
; correct interim state PlaceableDefinition.pending_signoff() already expects and handles.
;
; emitted_tags SET 2026-09-04 by the habitat-tiers ruling. Previously `[]` — every farm
; building was placeable decoration with no simulation meaning. `built` is emitted by
; EVERY placeable so one `HabitatLimit` on `built` excludes all of them, including
; buildings added later. SmallBarn also emits `barn` — the ordinary (non-large) barn
; source. See docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-habitat-tiers-design.md § 8.
; FOOTPRINT 1x1 -> 2x2, 2026-09-08 — TRIAL (human ruling), NOT a signed-off value.
; Open Question #18 (footprints & world dimensions) is still open; this is a look-pass so the
; human can judge the result before the downstream re-tuning is paid for.
;
; WHY: buildings read too small against a person. A villager normalises to exactly 1.0 tile
; height (WorldGrid.TILE_SIZE = 1.0) and every 1x1 building's mesh stood shorter than that. The
; model wrapper's scale was doubled to match (0.869309 -> 1.738618 long-axis target, which is
; Barn.tscn's existing 2x2 convention) — see the wrapper's own header for that half.
;
; `cost` IS DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED, per the same ruling. Consequence, noted not resolved:
; wood-per-tile-claimed drops 4x (Open Questions #8 cost table, #26 starting stockpile).
;
; KNOWN OUTSTANDING, DELIBERATELY NOT DONE HERE — a `built` HabitatLimit counts TILES, not
; buildings, so this building now contributes 4 `built` tiles where it contributed 1. That
; silently tightens every wild exclusion ceiling 4x: rabbit (both tiers, max_count = 2) is now
; excluded outright by a single building in scout radius, and deer's base tier and donkey's
; range tier (max_count = 1) become unreachable near any building at all. Fox, Stag and the deer
; herd tier are already at 0 and are unaffected. Those ceilings are tuning values and are the
; human's to re-rule.
